Hi Mike!

On 12/31/21 10:24, Mike Hosken wrote:
> Happy New Year,

Happy New Year!

> I sent an email to alpha@buildd.debian.org back in August I think. 

That address reaches the administrators of the buildd machines, not the Debian FTP
archive. I also think that there is currently no one behind this address. I may
ask Aurelien Jarno to add me to this alias.

> I suspect that itâs a file system error that has been synced with the other mirrors.
> Iâve come across a similar error before with hppa and Helge rebuilt the packages that
> were affected and it went away. Iâm not sure if thatâs the case here though. I do know
> that itâs been there for over a year now. I started setting up a mirror server for debian
> ports a year ago with this error, it was only in August when I put a new mirror server I
> online that it became an issue. Iâve been trying to resolve it since. 

What package was it that Helge rebuilt? I can rebuilt bustle, of course, although I think this
error is rather unusual.

> Any help with this issue would be very appreciated. 

Sure.

Adrian


